<pre><code>1) Getting used to git version controls 
2) Creating an initial blog with Quarto </code></pre>
</section>
<section id="what-i-learned" class="level2">
<h2 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="what-i-learned">What I learned</h2>
<pre><code>1) git clone (from a github link) 
2) git checkout -b "name_of_branch" :  create my own branch
3) modify the required file 
4) git status
5) git diff ( the differneces) 
6) git add . 
7) git commit -m "write what I have done"
8) git push 
9) git fetch origin (name of another branch)
10)git merge origin/the branch 
11) do the modification again , save , git add, git commit, push   </code></pre>


</section>

